{
  "rationale": "Use a small plant split into sensing and motion capability, then encode the exploration policy in specifications. The policy gives priority to forward progress in clear conditions, uses one-shot conservative recovery after obstacle events, avoids backward motion except as a brief front-obstacle escape, and returns to forward exploration immediately when path_clear is observed. Commit/recovery states self-loop on path_clear so the intended pulse is not preempted, while safety-critical obstacle events can redirect recovery.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate uncontrollable perception from controllable motion with two plant automata",
    "Use one policy automaton for clear exploration and obstacle-triggered recovery, plus one automaton to make full_rotate a last-resort only after repeated front blockage"
  ],
